---
title: "122 Numerical Control I - II"
code: "MAC-121"
category: "machine-technology"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Focuses on numerical control techniques in metal forming and machine processes. Includes theory and practice in lathe and milling machine computer numerical control program writing, setup and operation. Lecture 2 hour, Laboratory 3 hours, Total 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
